chat-title = Ask Breadator
chat-description = Bread-making questions answered from Breadator's knowledge base, with numbered sources, and every number from its calculators.
chat-lead = Ask a bread-making question. Answers rest on the knowledge base and number their sources; weights, temperatures and times come from Breadator's calculators.
chat-unavailable = The assistant is unavailable at the moment.
chat-signed-out = The assistant is free, but each answer costs the site a little: it needs an account, and each account gets 10 answers a day.
chat-sign-in = Sign in to ask a question
chat-privacy = Your question and the last turns of the conversation are sent to an AI model through OpenRouter, with zero data retention: the model providers keep nothing. Conversations stay in your account until you delete them, and the account's export and deletion include them. Your answer counts are kept until the end of the month under a one-way hash of your address, even after the account is deleted, so that the limits hold.
chat-warning = Answers can be wrong: check the sources, and treat anything marked (unsourced) with care.
